---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import PlannerCTA from '../../components/PlannerCTA.astro';

const faqSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: [
    {
      '@type': 'Question',
      name: 'Are propane heaters made specifically for sauna rooms?',
      acceptedAnswer: {
        '@type': 'Answer',
        text: 'Yes. Scandia currently lists 40,000 and 80,000 BTU gas sauna heaters with liquid-propane variants. Use only a heater and venting configuration approved for the exact sauna project, not a portable propane space heater.',
      },
    },
    {
      '@type': 'Question',
      name: 'Can I install a propane sauna heater myself?',
      acceptedAnswer: {
        '@type': 'Answer',
        text: 'The current Scandia installation guide requires licensed professional installation and directs buyers to a certified plumber or HVAC professional for gas pressure, installation, and connection. Local permits and inspections may also apply.',
      },
    },
    {
      '@type': 'Question',
      name: 'How do I size a propane sauna heater?',
      acceptedAnswer: {
        '@type': 'Answer',
        text: 'Start with the exact manufacturer manual, finished room dimensions, ceiling height, insulation, wall construction, outdoor temperature, venting plan, elevation, and gas pressure. Do not choose from BTU output alone.',
      },
    },
    {
      '@type': 'Question',
      name: 'Is propane cheaper than an electric sauna heater?',
      acceptedAnswer: {
        '@type': 'Answer',
        text: 'There is no universal answer. Compare the complete gas equipment, venting, controls, tank or supply work, licensed labor, permits, fuel delivery, and maintenance against the complete electrical-service and heater project.',
      },
    },
  ],
};
---
<Base
  title="Propane Sauna Heater Guide: Plan the Complete Gas System"
  description="Evaluate a propane sauna heater by current models, room range, venting, gas supply, controls, licensed installation, and complete project cost."
  canonical="/guides/propane-sauna-heater"
>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(faqSchema)} />

  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
    <header class="mb-8">
      <p class="text-sm text-amber-700 font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide mb-2">Gas heater planning guide</p>
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-stone-900 leading-tight mb-3">Propane Sauna Heaters: Plan the Whole Gas System</h1>
      <p class="text-stone-500">Reviewed August 2026 &middot; Planning guide, not installation instructions</p>
      <p class="text-lg text-stone-700 mt-4">Propane is a specialized sauna-heating path. The decision includes the exact heater, vent direction, combustion air, gas supply, controls, guard, room construction, permits, and licensed installation. It is not a portable-heater shortcut.</p>
    </header>

    <div class="bg-amber-50 border border-amber-200 rounded-xl p-5 mb-8">
      <h2 class="font-bold text-stone-900 mb-2">The market is too narrow for a credible "best" ranking</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-stone-700">Our current US manufacturer check found one documented gas-sauna line with liquid-propane variants: Scandia's 40,000 and 80,000 BTU heaters. That supports a project-fit comparison, not a ranked roundup. Confirm current availability and documentation directly with the manufacturer before designing around either model.</p>
    </div>

    <section class="mb-10" aria-labelledby="current-models">
      <h2 id="current-models" class="text-2xl font-bold text-stone-900 mb-4">Two current propane-capable heater formats</h2>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto border border-stone-200 rounded-lg">
        <table class="w-full min-w-[720px] text-sm border-collapse">
          <thead>
            <tr class="bg-stone-900 text-white">
              <th class="text-left p-3">Current model</th>
              <th class="text-left p-3">Published room range</th>
              <th class="text-left p-3">Current choices</th>
              <th class="text-left p-3">Verify before layout</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="text-stone-700">
            <tr class="bg-white">
              <td class="p-3 font-semibold border-b border-stone-200">Scandia 40K</td>
              <td class="p-3 border-b border-stone-200">84 to 616 cu. ft. in the current installation guide</td>
              <td class="p-3 border-b border-stone-200">Natural gas or liquid propane; standing pilot or piezo; horizontal or vertical vent</td>
              <td class="p-3 border-b border-stone-200">Room inputs, elevation, gas pressure, wall thickness, vent path, clearances, and required accessories</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="bg-stone-50">
              <td class="p-3 font-semibold border-b border-stone-200">Scandia 80K</td>
              <td class="p-3 border-b border-stone-200">450 to 1,680 cu. ft. in the current installation guide</td>
              <td class="p-3 border-b border-stone-200">Natural gas or liquid propane; standing pilot or piezo; horizontal or vertical vent</td>
              <td class="p-3 border-b border-stone-200">The same project inputs, plus the larger rough-in, guard, and clearance envelope</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p class="text-xs text-stone-500 mt-3">These ranges are manufacturer data, not our test results. The manual bases sizing on stated room assumptions, including a seven-foot ceiling. The ranges overlap, so room volume alone does not select the model.</p>
      <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-3 mt-5">
        <a href="https://scandiamfg.com/products/40k-btu-gas-sauna-heater" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="inline-flex min-h-12 items-center justify-center rounded-md bg-stone-900 px-5 py-3 font-semibold text-white hover:bg-stone-800">Check the current 40K listing</a>
        <a href="https://scandiamfg.com/products/80k-btu-gas-sauna-heater" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="inline-flex min-h-12 items-center justify-center rounded-md border border-stone-300 bg-white px-5 py-3 font-semibold text-stone-900 hover:border-stone-500">Check the current 80K listing</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <PlannerCTA
      source="propane_heater_after_current_models"
      heading="Put the gas-heater decision into a project brief"
      description="Capture the room, location, heat preference, utility status, budget, timeline, and installation needs before asking the manufacturer or a licensed contractor to review the project."
    />

    <section class="mt-10 mb-10" aria-labelledby="before-buying">
      <h2 id="before-buying" class="text-2xl font-bold text-stone-900 mb-4">Confirm these items before buying</h2>
      <ol class="list-decimal pl-5 space-y-4 text-stone-700">
        <li><strong>The finished room.</strong> Record inside length, width, height, wall construction, insulation, door fit, glazing, and whether the sauna is indoors or outdoors.</li>
        <li><strong>The exact fuel configuration.</strong> Liquid propane and natural-gas parts are not interchangeable assumptions. Confirm fuel, pressure, elevation, ignition, and the complete order configuration.</li>
        <li><strong>The vent direction.</strong> The current line offers horizontal and vertical configurations. The installation guide ties each to specific components and rough-in details.</li>
        <li><strong>Combustion and room air.</strong> The manufacturer requires adequate fresh air for safe operation and a properly installed, maintained venting system. Sauna room ventilation is a separate project requirement.</li>
        <li><strong>The licensed trades.</strong> Ask the manufacturer and local authority which HVAC, gas, electrical, permit, and inspection work applies. The current manual does not support self-installation.</li>
        <li><strong>The complete package.</strong> Confirm the heater, burner, controls, stones, back panel, flashing, vent components, guard, extensions, freight, and every field-supplied part.</li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-10" aria-labelledby="safety-boundary">
      <h2 id="safety-boundary" class="text-2xl font-bold text-stone-900 mb-4">Safety boundary</h2>
      <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-200 rounded-xl p-5">
        <p class="font-bold text-red-900 mb-2">Do not substitute a portable propane heater.</p>
        <p class="text-sm text-red-800 mb-3">A sauna reaches temperatures and operating conditions outside ordinary room-heater use. Use equipment documented for the sauna, follow the exact current manual, and have the gas and venting system installed and commissioned by qualified professionals.</p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-sm text-red-800">
          <li>The current Scandia manual warns that improper installation or operation can create carbon monoxide and flue-gas hazards.</li>
          <li>It requires outside venting, adequate combustion and ventilation air, external controls, local-code compliance, and a heater guard.</li>
          <li>For indoor installations, the manufacturer strongly recommends suitable carbon monoxide detectors near the appliance and in adjacent occupied spaces.</li>
          <li>A working vent does not make the risk disappear. Installation, operation, inspection, and maintenance all matter.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-10" aria-labelledby="cost-comparison">
      <h2 id="cost-comparison" class="text-2xl font-bold text-stone-900 mb-4">Compare project cost, not a universal session price</h2>
      <p class="text-stone-700 mb-4">The old version of this guide gave one propane-consumption range for every sauna. That was not defensible. The manufacturer says consumption changes with room construction, insulation, door fit, outdoor temperature, heater sizing, venting, and use.</p>
      <p class="text-stone-700 mb-5">Ask the gas supplier or installer to estimate fuel use from the selected model, local gas specification, expected firing pattern, and current delivered fuel price. Then compare the complete gas project with the electrical-service and wood-burning alternatives.</p>
      <a href="/tools/sauna-cost-calculator/" class="inline-flex min-h-12 items-center justify-center rounded-md bg-stone-900 px-5 py-3 font-semibold text-white hover:bg-stone-800">Build the complete project budget</a>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-10" aria-labelledby="fit-check">
      <h2 id="fit-check" class="text-2xl font-bold text-stone-900 mb-4">When propane deserves a closer look</h2>
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        <div class="border border-stone-200 rounded-lg bg-white p-5">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-stone-900 mb-3">Continue evaluating propane when...</h3>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-sm text-stone-700">
            <li>A documented gas sauna heater fits the exact room.</li>
            <li>A qualified professional accepts the gas, combustion-air, and venting path.</li>
            <li>Fuel storage, delivery, access, and local approvals are practical.</li>
            <li>The full installed scope is competitive with electric or wood.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="border border-stone-200 rounded-lg bg-white p-5">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-stone-900 mb-3">Choose another path when...</h3>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-sm text-stone-700">
            <li>You want a plug-in or portable setup.</li>
            <li>No qualified gas installer will approve the project.</li>
            <li>The room cannot accommodate the rough-in, guard, and clearances.</li>
            <li>Electric service or an approved wood system is simpler at full project cost.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-10" aria-labelledby="primary-sources">
      <h2 id="primary-sources" class="text-2xl font-bold text-stone-900 mb-4">Primary sources used</h2>
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        <a href="https://scandiamfg.com/products/40k-btu-gas-sauna-heater" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="block border border-stone-200 rounded-lg p-5 hover:border-amber-400">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-stone-900 mb-2">Scandia 40K product listing</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-stone-700">Current fuel, ignition, vent-direction, room-range, package, and professional-installation information.</p>
        </a>
        <a href="https://scandiamfg.com/products/80k-btu-gas-sauna-heater" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="block border border-stone-200 rounded-lg p-5 hover:border-amber-400">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-stone-900 mb-2">Scandia 80K product listing</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-stone-700">Current manufacturer listing for the larger gas-heater format and available configurations.</p>
        </a>
        <a href="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0468/8261/9555/files/SAUNA_GAS_HEATER_INSTALLATION_GUIDE_SCANDIA.pdf?v=1642457182" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="block border border-stone-200 rounded-lg p-5 hover:border-amber-400 md:col-span-2">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-stone-900 mb-2">Scandia gas-heater installation guide</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-stone-700">Manufacturer requirements for room inputs, sizing, venting, gas configuration, rough-in, controls, guard, safety, and professional installation.</p>
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-10" aria-labelledby="propane-faq">
      <h2 id="propane-faq" class="text-2xl font-bold text-stone-900 mb-4">Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <div class="space-y-5">
        <div><h3 class="font-bold text-stone-900 mb-1">Can I use a portable propane heater in a sauna?</h3><p class="text-stone-700">No. Choose equipment specifically documented for the sauna project and install it under the current manufacturer instructions and local requirements.</p></div>
        <div><h3 class="font-bold text-stone-900 mb-1">Which propane sauna heater is best?</h3><p class="text-stone-700">The current documented US selection is too narrow for a useful ranking. Compare the Scandia 40K and 80K configurations by the exact room, vent, fuel, rough-in, installer, and package requirements.</p></div>
        <div><h3 class="font-bold text-stone-900 mb-1">Can propane work indoors?</h3><p class="text-stone-700">The current manufacturer manual includes indoor-installation safety requirements. That does not mean every room or jurisdiction qualifies. A licensed professional and local authority must review the exact project.</p></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="bg-stone-50 border border-stone-200 rounded-xl p-6 mt-10">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-stone-900 mb-2">Compare the other heater paths</h2>
      <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm">
        <li><a href="/guides/best-sauna-heater/" class="text-amber-700 hover:underline">Open the heater planning hub</a></li>
        <li><a href="/guides/best-electric-sauna-heaters/" class="text-amber-700 hover:underline">Compare current electric formats</a></li>
        <li><a href="/guides/best-wood-burning-sauna-heaters/" class="text-amber-700 hover:underline">Compare wood-burning formats</a></li>
        <li><a href="/guides/sauna-ventilation/" class="text-amber-700 hover:underline">Coordinate room ventilation</a></li>
        <li><a href="/guides/sauna-heater-sizing-guide/" class="text-amber-700 hover:underline">Size from the exact room</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
